linton  and now what has pushed thus in Clint  Clint Sinclair story viral is these must  run packages right that are as the name  suggests they must be run on every  single one of Sinclair's affiliates or  at least the one Sinclair determines  need to run it and very often these  segments are nothing but a regurgitation  of conservative talking points filled  with Trump era cliches like snow flake  and fake news but I actually am making  the case that the problem is way deeper  than propaganda and the political bias  of the content towards Trump and skewed  towards the right the entire  infrastructure is a systemic problem  because it completely undermines the  purpose of local news when Sinclair  sends out these mandatory political  content packages and they force-feed the  national discussion into so-called local  news they are basically saying well it  looks like local news but it's really  not local news and the reason that  that's an acute problem is that  Americans believe that their local news  is more trustworthy than national news  and the reason why is obvious right we  think locally we live mostly locally and  so we're predisposed to believe that the  material we get from our local anchors  is more authentic more relevant to our  community than the national stuff and to  a degree it's true or at least in theory  it's true so when people don't realize  that their local news is carefully  crafted propaganda from this national  company Sinclair is able to exploit the  faith that many news consumers have in  their supposed local media when they're  actually just selling us an  assembly-line right-wing message and  this is hugely destructive because in  the not so long run it's going to mean  the demise of regional diversity on  television and even local TV is going to  look identical across the country more  than it already does in that format  which I've actually talked about before  and I recently read a defense of  Sinclair's practices because you  can always find someone willing to  defend just about any practice david har  say ani said that sinclair is doing  quote advocacy journalism and that  that's valuable and that it's good to  have competing biases in society so that  all views are heard and can be  challenged or something along those  lines and sure I mean in principle he's  right we want a marketplace of ideas and  we can evaluate ideas and decide what  makes sense and what should prevail but  the problem isn't that a biased media  company is being biased it's the lack of  transparency it's the bamboozling of  viewers that's happening when Sinclair  monopolizes local markets and people  don't even understand what it is that  they're seeing and I've explained before  I've been talking for years that one of  the despicable things that Fox News does  is they blur the lines between what's  news and what's opinion journalism and  you wonder as you watch am i watching a  report right now or am i watching a  commentary and it's by design that you  often can't tell or that fox news mixes  them together and Sinclair is doing  another version of that am i watching  local news or am i watching force fed  national talking points produced by  someone who's cozy with the president  and struck a deal with Jared Kushner  packaged to be delivered by my local  anchors who I think have my community  sort of as their priority so what can be  done about this I genuinely have no idea  I mentioned that Sinclair is looking to  buy Tribune media that's currently being  considered by the FCC we can't really  count on the current administration's  FCC to stop it we've got FCC chairman  and Trump appointee Ajit PI being  investigated by his own agency and yet  still the odds are in Sinclair's favor  that the FCC is not going to get in the  way of the purchase of Tribune media so  if there is a hope it's going to be  found far from corporate media and the  silver lining is that the Internet has  plenty of independent journalists and  news outlets and yes I am one of those  and certainly this is a circumstance  where  I stand to gain but we also all stand to  gain from more diversity and voices we  need to be supporting other models of  funding that enabled the audience to  actually find and decide what are the  voices and messages that actually  reflect their beliefs or their ideals  and cater to their interests and values  and morals and and the real silver  lining here is that which is that  hopefully the Sinclair media scandal  wakes people up to the reality that  you've got to support independent media  when so-called local news stations are  increase increasingly owned and managed  either by the big news networks or by  media conglomerates like Sinclair we  need to look elsewhere and that's why  we're working to expand the show and  doing all of the other things that you  know that we are doing send me your  thoughts about my commentary and article  on Sinclair it's on pluralist we're  linking to the article in the video  description for the youtube clip for  this story the video you just finished  watching was made possible by you  through the membership program you can  sign up for membership at david  pakman.com slash membership we are  viewer supported independent media you  can use the coupon code  I voted 17 for a 40% discount off of  your membership
 

